# AdGuard Home Configuration
# Copy to .env and customize

# ── Network Settings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AdGuard listens on all interfaces by default
# No environment variables needed for basic setup

# ── Authentik SSO (Optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AdGuard Home does not natively support OIDC/SSO
# Authentication is protected via Caddy forward-auth to Authentik
# This means only users in homelab-admin can access the AdGuard admin UI

# ── DNS Upstream Servers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are configured in AdGuard UI, documented here for reference:
#
# Recommended upstream DNS servers (configure in UI):
# - Cloudflare: https://dns.cloudflare.com/dns-query (DoH)
# - Quad9: https://dns.quad9.net/dns-query (DoH)
# - Cloudflare: tls://1.1.1.1 (DoT)
#
# Bootstrap DNS (for resolving DoH/DoT hostnames):
# - 1.1.1.1
# - 9.9.9.9

# ── Query Logging ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Query log retention (days) - configured in UI
# Recommended: 7 days for privacy and storage

# ── Notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# After deploying AdGuard Home:
# 1. Complete initial setup at http://adguard.home
# 2. Set admin username/password (Authentik SSO is secondary layer)
# 3. Configure upstream DNS servers
# 4. Enable DNS rewrites for *.home domains (see README)
# 5. Update router DHCP to use AdGuard as DNS server
